---
interface Props { practiceHref?: string }
const { practiceHref } = Astro.props;
const opening = "I suggest a 15-minute weekly project check-in. It would give us a regular place to discuss questions.";
---

<section class="section wrap brief-example" id="brief-example" aria-labelledby="brief-example-title">
  <div class="example-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">A coaching move you can try</p>
    <h2 id="brief-example-title">Give the listener<br /><em>a decision.</em></h2>
    <p>A recommendation can be clear while the next step is still missing. Read this update to a project partner. What are you asking them to do?</p>
    <p class="example-boundary">Fictional practice example. The timings and scenario are invented for this exercise.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="example-pair">
    <div class="first-attempt">
      <h3><span aria-hidden="true">01 / </span>Initial attempt</h3>
      <blockquote><p>{opening}</p><p>That is what I wanted to share.</p></blockquote>
      <p class="coaching-question"><strong>Pause here.</strong> What could the partner say or do next? Try your own closing sentence before opening the revision.</p>
    </div>
    <details class="example-revision">
      <summary>See one possible revision <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
      <div class="revision-body">
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">02 / </span>Change only the ending</h3>
        <blockquote><p>{opening}</p><p><strong>Would you join a two-week trial and then help us decide whether to continue?</strong></p></blockquote>
        <p class="revision-reason">The opening stays the same. The new ending gives this project partner a specific invitation and a decision to revisit.</p>
        <div class="listener-check">
          <h3>Check what came through</h3>
          <p>Ask the listener: “What was the recommendation, and what action or decision was requested?” If either is unclear, revise that part and try again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <div class="example-next">
    <p>Try it with a safe scenario of your own. Adapt the request to your listener; use only facts you can support.</p>
    {practiceHref && <a class="text-link" href={practiceHref}>Try the free 10-minute briefing practice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .example-heading { max-width: 720px; }
  h2 { margin-top: 18px; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 58px); font-weight: 600; }
  .example-heading > p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-top: 22px; }
  .example-boundary { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .example-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; gap: 28px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .first-attempt { padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 36px); background: var(--wash); border-top: 3px solid var(--line); }
  h3 { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: -.02em; font-weight: 700; }
  h3 span { color: var(--blue); }
  blockquote { margin: 20px 0 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.6; }
  blockquote p + p { margin-top: 18px; }
  .coaching-question, .revision-reason { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px; }
  .example-revision { border: 1px solid var(--blue); border-top-width: 3px; }
  summary { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 20px; padding: 22px; min-height: 64px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--blue); font-weight: 700; list-style: none; }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary span { font-size: 24px; }
  details[open] summary span { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .revision-body { padding: 6px clamp(22px, 3vw, 36px) 30px; }
  blockquote strong { background: #fff2b8; box-decoration-break: clone; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; }
  .listener-check { margin-top: 28px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listener-check p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .example-next { margin-top: 28px; max-width: 720px; }
  .example-next .text-link { margin-top: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .example-pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 22px; } }
</style>
